From 66550b7438b15cb9490e18373ab7c8e05534e489 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Passerelle contributors <passerelle@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:51:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] main: choose the transport, defaulting to the
 architecture

An x86_64 guest gets its share from QEMU's -virtfs, which creates a
virtio-9p-pci device; an ARM64 virt guest from -device virtio-9p-device,
which is virtio-mmio. fs-9p now picks the matching backend from the
architecture it was built for, and -o transport=mmio|pci overrides that
for a machine that does not follow the rule (an x86_64 microvm guest, for
instance, whose devices are MMIO).

The option is documented where the consistency test looks for it: the use
message and docs/user/reference.md. The reference page also says that
-o irq= only applies to virtio-mmio, since the PCI transport takes its
interrupt from MSI-X or from the firmware's INTx assignment.

CHANGELOG gains the user-visible additions: the PCI transport, the new
option, the x86_64 target and the host tests for the decoder.
